---
import { ecosystem } from '../../data/portfolio.js';
---
<section class="slide soft" id="ecosystem" data-section>
  <div class="slide-canvas"><div class="canvas-inner">
    <div class="ecosystem-layout">
      <article class="dark-story">
        <span class="story-index">PRODUCT ECOSYSTEM</span>
        <h2>Product is the coordination layer between business, technology and operations.</h2>
        <p>Enterprise products rarely succeed through a feature alone. They connect the user journey with workflows, data, integrations, controls, intelligence and operational readiness.</p>
        <div class="story-points"><span>Customer and business problem → measurable outcome</span><span>Product journey and workflow across multiple systems</span><span>AI / GenAI opportunity in real business processes</span><span>Automation, data, operations and compliance readiness</span></div>
      </article>
      <div class="ecosystem-grid">
        {ecosystem.map(([title, text, tags], index) => <article class="eco-card"><span class="card-number">0{index + 1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p><small>{tags}</small></article>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>
